# CODEOWNERS
#
# Auto-requests review from the listed owner(s) on any pull request that
# touches a matching path. See docs/governance.md for the full explanation,
# including why "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection is
# inert until a second collaborator with write access exists.
#
# --- Tier 0 baseline: one catch-all line covers almost every repo --------
# Every repository, regardless of tier, gets this line (see docs/tiers.md's
# Tier 0 checklist). Replace @<maintainer-handle> with the actual GitHub
# handle. Do not add path-specific rows below this for a single-maintainer
# repo — there's no second owner to route reviews to, so extra lines are
# pure noise no matter how large the repo is.

* @<maintainer-handle>

# --- Once there are multiple maintainers: path-specific ownership --------
# Uncomment and adapt once more than one person has write access, each
# covering a different area. The trigger is headcount, not tier by itself —
# this commonly shows up around Tier 2+, since that's when repos tend to
# accumulate a second maintainer, but a smaller repo that unusually gains
# one should adopt this early too. More specific patterns override the
# catch-all above; on a tie, the last matching line in the file wins, so
# keep the catch-all first and put overrides after it.
#
# /infra/              @<infra-owner-handle>
# /docs/               @<docs-owner-handle>
# *.sql                 @<db-owner-handle>
